# Stage 9 finalist calibration comparison — implementation record

## Scope and status

- Added `mi_stage9_finalist_calibration.py` for the provisional candidate pairs:
  DEATH_BINARY (TabPFN 3.5, CatBoost tuned), ZSN (TabPFN 3.5, Random Forest
  tuned), and FIBR_PREDS (Extra Trees preliminary, Random Forest preliminary).
- The script uses only Stage 1 development artifacts and saved development
  tuning settings. It contains no held-out data paths and refuses to overwrite
  a Stage 9 output directory.
- No Stage 9 output directory has been created. The user approved the
  development-only nested fit run, with no test access, identical
  target-level outer folds, calibrator training confined to outer training
  data, raw/calibrated AP, AUROC, Brier, and Log Loss, preserved prior
  outputs, and fold-level records. No dependencies or weights were
  downloaded; the existing TabPFN cache was confirmed present (876,028,347
  bytes).
- No prior stage outputs, task checklists, or handoff files were modified.

## Method design

- Five seed-42 stratified outer folds estimate development-only performance.
- Within each outer training partition, four-fold stratified OOF base
  probabilities train a sigmoid/Platt calibrator. Each candidate is then
  refit on the complete outer training partition and scored once on the
  untouched outer validation fold. All learned imputation/encoding remains in
  the existing tree model pipelines. TabPFN uses its existing native
  categorical handling.
- Tuned candidate settings are taken from the saved fold-specific Stage 3 or
  Stage 6 development tuning records for the corresponding outer fold; they
  are not retuned in this calibration comparison. Since these settings were
  selected using the full outer training partition, inner calibration scores
  are not fully independent of labels used in setting selection. The untouched
  outer validation fold still evaluates the full procedure; final fitting
  should freeze or reselect hyperparameters inside its calibration folds.
  Preliminary candidates use their recorded fixed defaults.
- Outputs, when authorized and run, will include candidate OOF predictions,
  fold metrics, pooled summaries, fold aggregates, warnings, and a concise
  report. AP remains the primary metric; AUROC, Brier, Log Loss, ECE,
  calibration slope/intercept diagnostics, and fixed-0.5 threshold metrics are
  supplemental. Candidate/model/calibration/threshold choices remain
  provisional until separately reviewed and frozen.

## Checks so far

- `.venv/bin/python -m py_compile mi_stage9_finalist_calibration.py` — passed
  after the final cleanup.
- `git diff --check -- mi_stage9_finalist_calibration.py
  logs/2026-11-05_stage9_finalist_calibration.log` — passed.
- First run command, after user approval of the nested development-only fits:
  `env SKB_DATA_DIRECTORY=/private/tmp/skrub-stage8
  TABPFN_MODEL_CACHE_DIR=/private/tmp/tabpfn-stage8-cache
  MPLCONFIGDIR=/private/tmp/mi-stage9-mplconfig
  .venv/bin/python mi_stage9_finalist_calibration.py`.
- The run was manually interrupted after approximately 30 seconds when the
  independent reviewer found static issues. It stopped during the first
  TabPFN inner-fold prediction with `KeyboardInterrupt`; a candidate fit had
  started, but no complete candidate fold evaluation finished and no output
  directory/artifacts were written (output writing occurs only after all fits
  and alignment checks). This interruption followed the
  user-approved compute scope and is recorded, not a model result.
- Planned evaluation size: six candidate/target pairs × five outer folds ×
  (four inner calibration fits + one outer refit) = 150 base-model fits,
  including 50 TabPFN fits. Independent static review initially failed on the
  expected-ID alignment and calibration-setting caveat; both were corrected.
  Fresh independent static recheck passed before the full rerun resumed.
- Second run attempt used the same command and environment. It completed the
  DEATH_BINARY TabPFN nested candidate (25 fits) and stopped on the first
  CatBoost tuned inner fit with exit 1 after about four minutes. CatBoost
  requires `classifier__cat_features=stage6.CATEGORICAL` as a fit argument on
  its sklearn pipeline; without it, the fixed missing-category token was
  treated as numeric. No output directory or artifacts were written. The
  script now passes the required fit metadata through a shared helper. This
  failed run and the 25 completed TabPFN fits are retained as run evidence;
  they are not reported as candidate results because the full candidate
  comparison did not complete.
- The focused CatBoost fit correction passed independent static recheck before
  the successful compute run.
- The complete approved rerun then succeeded with the same command and
  temporary Skrub/TabPFN/Matplotlib directories. Approximate process wall time
  was 17 minutes 40 seconds (no internal timer was added). It completed all
  150 base-model fits and all 30 candidate/outer-fold evaluations and wrote
  outputs only after validation.
- TabPFN emitted the same captured `UserWarning` in its ten candidate outer
  folds (five per target): CPU execution with more than 1,000 samples may be
  slow. No other model fit warnings were captured. `warnings.csv` preserves
  these ten rows. No dependencies or model weights were downloaded during
  the run.
- Output checks passed: 8,160 unique OOF target/model/ID rows, 30 fold rows
  (five per candidate), 12 pooled summaries, six fold aggregates, and ten
  warning rows. A read-only verifier checked actual eligible development IDs,
  labels, exact seed-42 outer fold membership, finite/bounded probabilities,
  and recomputed AP/AUROC/Brier/Log Loss for both probability stages on every
  fold (294 checks passed). The first verifier pass used unclipped raw
  probabilities for Log Loss and differed by at most 2.6e-8; rerunning with
  the script's declared 1e-6 probability clipping passed all 294 checks. The
  import-based version check initially hit Skrub's default home-directory
  permission; package metadata checks then passed without importing packages.
- Environment: Python 3.14.7 on macOS 15.5 arm64; NumPy 2.5.4, pandas 3.1.0,
  scikit-learn 1.9.1, CatBoost 1.2.10, TabPFN 9.2.0, PyTorch 2.15.0, and
  MLX 0.32.4.
- Added `stage9_results.md` as a new companion result artifact derived from
  the completed outputs; it reports fold mean/sample-SD AP, AUROC, Brier, and
  Log Loss before/after sigmoid, plus pooled OOF ECE/slope/intercept. No prior
  stage output or Stage 9 numeric result was changed.
- Independent static review passed before the successful run. Independent
  generated-artifact review also passed: it verified all 30 candidate folds,
  all 8,160 OOF rows against development IDs/labels/folds, and recomputed raw
